Hi Luis, thanks again. <div><br></div><div>So to be clear:<div>1. I don&#39;t have to load dartR again (with library(dartR) ) after running &quot;

<i>gl.install.vanilla.dartR() &quot; </i>, correct?</div><div>2. Ok, thanks. But what type of bug does the 

<i>gl.install.vanilla.dartR  </i>function have? Because I am currently using the most updated version of dartR (2.0.4), but I installed it as such:</div><div><i>install.packages(dartR)</i></div><div><i>library(dartR)</i></div><div><i>gl.install.vanilla.dartR()</i><br></div><div><br></div><div>I only found this previous post mentioning a bug in the <i>gl.install.vanilla.dartR </i>function: <a href="https://groups.google.com/g/dartr/c/dvQ08sgTd5U/m/UuiYMdyQAAAJ" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/g/dartr/c/dvQ08sgTd5U/m/UuiYMdyQAAAJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792458500033000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2iSjEm42wxoToGw7cJn2Cb">https://groups.google.com/g/dartr/c/dvQ08sgTd5U/m/UuiYMdyQAAAJ</a></div><div>Was the problem only that the <i>gl.install.vanilla.dartR()</i>  function was not actually installing the developer version?</div><div><br></div><div>Should I then use the code you proposed in that post to install the dev version &amp; also the full CRAN dartR version? --&gt;</div><div>devtools::install_github(&quot;green-striped-gecko/dartR&quot;, ref = &quot;beta&quot;, dependencies = TRUE)<br></div><div><br></div><div>In your dartR manual, it states that the<i> gl.install.vanilla.dartR()</i> &quot;<u>installs all missing and required packages for your version of dartR.</u>&quot;...</div><div>So, to install all missing packages (not installed through install.packages(&quot;dartR&quot;)?? ), I should use the following?:</div><div><i>devtools::install_github(&quot;green-striped-gecko/dartR&quot;, ref = &quot;CRAN&quot;, dependencies = TRUE)</i> # or ref=&quot;<i>master</i>&quot;?<br></div><div><br></div><div>Sorry for the constant questions...but it&#39;s just to ensure I am using the correct version and avoiding known bugs as much as possible..</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks a lot!</div><div>Best,</div><div>Gabriella</div><div><br></div><div><i><br></i></div><div><i><br></i></div><div><br><br></div></div>
